course: dictionary
lesson: 8965
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must use the context to find the right one. Read the words around the word and ask which meaning fits best. The word sin is a good example.
explain: «An accident is not a sin; hiding it can grow into one.» Here sin means an act that breaks God's law or a religious rule. Faiths such as Christianity, Islam and Judaism teach about sin and forgiveness. The word accident is set against sin, which is a clue that the two are different.
explain: «It's a sin to waste good food» is a different meaning. This is informal talk, and it means something is a terrible shame. In maths, sin is short for sine, a function used with angles in triangles. The sentence and its topic tell you which meaning is meant.
fact: Sin can be a noun (a sin, sins) or a verb (sin, sinned, sinning).
fact: In religion, a sin is an act that breaks God's law or a religious rule.
fact: Informally, «It's a sin to waste good food» means it is a terrible shame.
fact: In maths, sin is short for sine, a button on a calculator.
fact: «Ugly as sin» means very ugly, and «live in sin» is an old phrase.
exercise: «It's a sin to waste good food.» What does sin mean here? | An act that breaks God's law | *Something that seems very wrong or a shame | A sine button on a calculator | A kind of fish
exercise: In maths, sin is short for what? | sigh | single | sinus | *sine
exercise: «Whoever conceals their sins does not prosper.» Find and copy one word that means hides. | prosper | renounces | mercy | *conceals
test: «Christians believe God meets confession with mercy.» What does mercy suggest? | Punishment | Shouting | Lost property | *Kindness and forgiveness
test: What does «ugly as sin» mean? | Very kind | *Very ugly | Very old | Very quiet
exam: Which meaning of sin fits «An accident is not a sin; hiding it can grow into one»? | Very ugly | A calculator button used with triangles | Something that is a shame to waste | *An act that breaks God's law or a religious rule
